WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:06.980
Can you imagine how much easier business could
be if you and I could be in seven different

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:08.370
places at the same time?

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:12.920
Now obviously today we don't have that technology,
so until that happens, we've got to figure

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:14.410
out how to build remotely.

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:20.050
Today in this episode, I will talk to you
about how you can lead multiple teams in multiple

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:23.190
locations and be effective at the same time.

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:25.030
So, let's first start off by looking at this
here.

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:27.200
I'm going to give you two examples.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:33.570
One, why is it that most entrepreneurs only
do well with businesses that are within 30

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:34.570
yards of them?

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:35.570
What do I mean by this?

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:36.629
You run an office.

00:00:36.629 --> 00:00:37.629
Everyone's around you.

00:00:37.629 --> 00:00:40.429
It's about 30 yards here, 20 yards this way.

00:00:40.429 --> 00:00:42.559
You do the math and it's about 3,000 square
feet.

00:00:42.559 --> 00:00:43.860
And we can manage that.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:47.850
But we have a very hard time building remotely
nationally.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:49.910
So let's look at the pros and cons of each
one.

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:51.710
Pros of building within 30 yards.

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:53.780
One, lots of control.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:58.339
So, most entrepreneurs start off being control
freaks, for the most part.

00:00:58.339 --> 00:01:01.199
Not everybody, but for the most part, the
whole reason why you become an entrepreneur

00:01:01.199 --> 00:01:03.960
is you want to control your destiny and all
these other things.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.240
You also like to control what everybody does,
right?

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:09.230
So the pro is, you get to see everybody.

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:11.100
You get to drive everybody.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:14.890
You get to see the heartbeat because you're
around everybody so they feel the heartbeat.

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:16.750
You are the heartbeat.

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:17.750
Accountability.

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:20.460
It's easy when somebody's doing something,
asking where they're at.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:24.250
I can be walking in the hallway, and somebody
walks by and I say, "Hey, where are you at

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.250
for today?

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:26.320
What did you do today?"

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:27.320
Quick fix.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.420
There's an issue I can solve that issue right
off the bat.

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:31.510
Sometimes, there's office politics.

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:33.220
There's arguments going on.

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:34.220
There's differences.

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:35.220
There's friction.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:38.300
If I know it, I can say, "Let's have a quick
30-minute meeting" and that can be solved.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:39.790
So, quick fix.

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:44.330
Low turnover, because the closer they are
to you, turnover will be typically lower.

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:46.360
However, there's one big con.

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:50.590
The big con is exponential growth, which means
expansion.

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:55.780
So the more you control, whatever you control
more, grows less.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:02:00.890
Whatever you control more has less possibility
of exponentially growing and exploding.

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:04.950
And you don't mind doing that in the business,
but you also got to make sure you do it properly

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:09.200
from the beginning, so when it explodes, it's
exploding on the right fundamentals instead

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.700
of just exploding without having any kind
of standards and expectation to grow on.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.299
So, now, remote, pros and cons.

00:02:16.299 --> 00:02:18.459
Pro, you can scale.

00:02:18.459 --> 00:02:22.840
Multiple locations, international, national,
East coast, West coast, mid-west, south, it

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:23.840
doesn't matter.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:25.209
I can be all over the place.

00:02:25.209 --> 00:02:30.719
I can build independent leaders, attract different
personalities, because some people like to

00:02:30.719 --> 00:02:33.209
be remotely running their own businesses.

00:02:33.209 --> 00:02:37.519
They kind of want to be left alone, so those
personalities, the solopreneurs will be turned

00:02:37.519 --> 00:02:38.709
on by this.

00:02:38.709 --> 00:02:45.599
The cons - lack of accountability, lack of
emotional connection, boredom, sometimes people

00:02:45.599 --> 00:02:49.920
that are working off site, remotely from you,
they get bored because they're not being sold

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:53.709
the vision regularly, so they don't see it
on a daily basis, and they get bored.

00:02:53.709 --> 00:02:56.170
And last but not least, low retention.

00:02:56.170 --> 00:03:00.269
So you have low turnover is a pro here [30
yards], higher retention.

00:03:00.269 --> 00:03:02.150
You have low retention here [remote].

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:07.700
So now, someone could say, Well, Pat, this
is exactly why I prefer doing this [30 yards].

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:12.569
This is exactly why I only want to build within
my vicinity, my office, everyone's close to

00:03:12.569 --> 00:03:13.569
me.

00:03:13.569 --> 00:03:15.279
I don't want to build remotely.

00:03:15.279 --> 00:03:19.870
I will challenge you there and tell you from
my own experience, for the first five years

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:23.379
of my business, I only built within 30 yards.

00:03:23.379 --> 00:03:24.420
Because I wanted control.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:27.640
Because I had to know exactly what everything
was doing.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:28.640
And then I made adjustments.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:32.930
I made a lot of mistakes but finally figured
out what things you have to do for this to

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:34.810
go from here [30 yards], to here [remote].

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:37.659
So let me explain to you a solution.

00:03:37.659 --> 00:03:44.639
#1, before you open up anyone to be remote,
in another place, always have a two to four

00:03:44.639 --> 00:03:49.959
week on the job training, field training,
shadowing, whatever you want to call it.

00:03:49.959 --> 00:03:52.769
Have somebody come and watch how everything's
being run.

00:03:52.769 --> 00:03:58.360
Have them watch how things being the systems,
the protocols, the sales flow.

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:02.239
Anything that is a skill that can be passed
through somebody else, have them sit through

00:04:02.239 --> 00:04:03.239
it.

00:04:03.239 --> 00:04:07.799
I used to tell myself, I don't do any behavior
unless if somebody's sitting in that office

00:04:07.799 --> 00:04:10.390
with me, to watch exactly what I'm doing.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:14.700
If I'm making phone calls, I want five people
around me to see how I'm making those sales

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:15.700
calls.

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:17.650
What's the purpose if I'm making the calls
all by myself?

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:21.019
If I'm making a sales presentation, I want
sitting right next to me.

00:04:21.019 --> 00:04:25.060
If I'm making a conference call with attorneys
and everybody, then I want somebody sitting

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:27.199
right next to me, or being on the call with
me.

00:04:27.199 --> 00:04:31.349
I want as much exposure to be with my team,
because I want to do on the job training.

00:04:31.349 --> 00:04:32.800
I want more PBDs out there.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.819
I want more leaders being developed out there,
right?

00:04:34.819 --> 00:04:38.889
And the way you do it, there's one thing to
give them a manual and say, Here you go!

00:04:38.889 --> 00:04:40.630
Go learn how to sell and go get 'em!

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:42.169
The best way to do it, go get.

00:04:42.169 --> 00:04:43.530
. . it's not going to work.

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:44.810
On the job training #1.

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:46.550
#2, build leaders.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:47.580
Focus on developing leaders.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:55.470
And the way you build leaders that build remotely,
any remote office or multiple locations that

00:04:55.470 --> 00:05:01.150
succeed, anything that succeeds, I guarantee
you it succeeds because there's a leader leading

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:02.150
that.

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:03.150
If there's no leader, it doesn't succeed.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.720
It's always the case.

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:05.720
Always the case.

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:10.349
You take any company that's extremely successful,
it is extremely successful because they've

00:05:10.349 --> 00:05:12.790
done a very good job building leaders.

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:16.440
Next, this is the part most people don't want
to do.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:22.800
Most 30-yard type of leaders, which I call
30-yard type of leaders who are control freaks,

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:25.830
they don't like to go visit other offices.

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:28.790
Because typically this [30-yard] becomes their
priority, which it's supposed to be because

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:33.949
this is your hub, but one of these [remote]
could end up being better than your hub, if

00:05:33.949 --> 00:05:35.440
you do quarterly visits.

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:37.490
So I like to go visit quarterly.

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:42.520
The reason why I've always liked quarterly
visits is one, I stay connected to the heartbeat,

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:48.639
two, I'm building relationships, three, I
can see things I need to fix, if there's issues,

00:05:48.639 --> 00:05:52.940
if there's challenges that come up, if I go
in a place and I notice there's a leak here

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:56.400
we've got to fix, oh I'm so glad we got here
before this one was going to be.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:58.879
. . oh, they were having issues financially
in this area.

00:05:58.879 --> 00:06:03.250
Oh, they had a terminal issue going on here
with the business that they weren't even using

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:07.419
this that could lead into a ton of complaints
that this could have caused a lot of headaches

00:06:07.419 --> 00:06:09.430
later on and I'm so glad I did that.

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:11.190
But it requires quarterly visits.

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:14.050
So someone may say, "Pat, what if I have nine
offices?

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:15.379
What if I have five locations?

00:06:15.379 --> 00:06:16.379
What if I have this going on?

00:06:16.379 --> 00:06:17.530
What if I have that going on?"

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:24.000
Use the 90/10 rule or the Pareto theory, the
80/20 rule, spend 80% of your time on the

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.910
top 20% of performing offices.

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:30.990
And develop them and develop those remote
businesses that show up because you can build

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:35.819
them into stronger leaders who can potentially
develop other locations as well.

00:06:35.819 --> 00:06:42.539
Next, two times a year do annual gatherings
and conventions, where everybody comes together.

00:06:42.539 --> 00:06:44.310
Say you have four offices.

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:47.160
Four offices all come together twice a year.

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:48.259
Everybody sees everybody.

00:06:48.259 --> 00:06:50.560
Because people learn from other offices.

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:52.610
People see what other leaders are doing better
than them.

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:57.729
They're collaborating, they're learning, cross-pollinating,
there's a lot of strong strengths coming together.

00:06:57.729 --> 00:07:01.260
And this person wasn't good in this, and this
girl was better at it than him.

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:02.260
He learns from her.

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:04.830
She wasn't good at this, that this guy's very
good at.

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:05.830
They learn from together.

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:07.759
There's a lot of strength that comes out of
that.

00:07:07.759 --> 00:07:09.960
Next, weekly accountability calls.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:13.340
Literally weekly accountability calls where
it could go for 90 minutes.

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:14.360
And this is how the call starts.

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:16.750
So, hey, what'd you do this past week?

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:20.190
The way I like to do accountability calls,
I like to do accountability calls based on

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:21.880
two different behaviors.

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:25.370
One is behavior, one is measurable figures.

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:28.759
Each one of them typically have four things
I want to ask for.

00:07:28.759 --> 00:07:33.110
So four behaviors, so could be this week I
sent this many emails.

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:34.219
I made this many calls.

00:07:34.219 --> 00:07:37.370
I did this many appointments that are these
types of sales.

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:39.790
I made these many appointments that are this
type of thing.

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:41.360
But I want four activities.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:43.669
So activity, results.

00:07:43.669 --> 00:07:45.580
I brought on board this many employees.

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:47.400
I sold this many of this product.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:50.629
We did this much in our office in volume and
we did this.

00:07:50.629 --> 00:07:51.629
Okay, great.

00:07:51.629 --> 00:07:55.490
Four activities and results, on a weekly basis.

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:59.340
We start off with those offices leaders that
are running remotely.

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:01.689
Give me these reports on what they did.

00:08:01.689 --> 00:08:05.020
Then I ask what worked for everybody this
week.

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:07.400
Share with the rest of us so we can learn.

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:08.479
We did this at our office.

00:08:08.479 --> 00:08:09.479
We did that in our office.

00:08:09.479 --> 00:08:10.479
We did this.

00:08:10.479 --> 00:08:11.479
Phenomenal.

00:08:11.479 --> 00:08:13.009
Next, what would you like to process?

00:08:13.009 --> 00:08:18.440
Then we literally for an hour process any
subject they want to process together, so

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:22.150
everyone learns from one another, we address
issues there.

00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:23.680
We bring leaders bulletin there.

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:27.050
There's challenges, there's issues were solved,
boom.

00:08:27.050 --> 00:08:28.409
Next week again.

00:08:28.409 --> 00:08:29.629
Next week again.

00:08:29.629 --> 00:08:30.629
Next week again.

00:08:30.629 --> 00:08:32.280
A weekly accountability going.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:34.060
Next, daily reports.

00:08:34.060 --> 00:08:40.320
The newer the leader is that's running a remote
office, the more daily reports I want.

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:44.480
The more of a veteran leader this person becomes,
that they're running it independently, I only

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:45.810
need weekly reporting.

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:49.029
But if you're newer, I need daily reporting,
because I don't trust you yet.

00:08:49.029 --> 00:08:50.589
I don't know who you are yet.

00:08:50.589 --> 00:08:53.090
I don't trust you running the operation all
by yourself yet.

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:54.490
I need daily reporting.

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:56.519
Daily reporting could be the same thing.

00:08:56.519 --> 00:08:59.240
How much was your activity, what happened,
what did you learn?

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:01.450
Here's what I did today, bop, bop, bop, bop.

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:04.290
Great, three minute email sent, I know.

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:05.389
And I look at it, okay, cool.

00:09:05.389 --> 00:09:06.550
Good, I look, all good.

00:09:06.550 --> 00:09:07.820
There's a red sign here, red signal.

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:08.820
Let me call them.

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:10.329
Then I call you up.

00:09:10.329 --> 00:09:11.510
then I send you a text.

00:09:11.510 --> 00:09:13.620
Hey, you told me this in an email here, what
do you mean by that?

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:14.620
Can you elaborate?

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:15.720
Did you figure out how to do this?

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:16.920
Hey, I think you need to read this book.

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:18.330
I think you need to watch this video.

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:21.279
There's still education going on there.

00:09:21.279 --> 00:09:23.560
Following, two times a year, fun trips.

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:24.590
What could be a fun trip?

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:26.960
A fun trip could be a BBQ together.

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:31.139
A fun trip could be I put a contest together,
we're going to go to a cruise.

00:09:31.139 --> 00:09:33.110
We're going to go to a trip.

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:34.620
We're going to go Disneyworld.

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:35.820
We're going to go to Disneyland.

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:38.590
We're going to go to, I don't know, a show.

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:43.089
We're going to go to a basketball game, a
sporting event, whatever it is, you put it

00:09:43.089 --> 00:09:49.250
twice a year that something fun happens, where
they see you not in business, I'm your boss

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:50.800
you better listen to me.

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:53.440
No, it's just let it loose, let's hang out,
let's talk.

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:54.770
Let's break bread, let's talk.

00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:55.770
What's going on?

00:09:55.770 --> 00:09:56.770
Tell me about your family.

00:09:56.770 --> 00:09:57.770
What's going on with your life?

00:09:57.770 --> 00:10:00.470
You do that a couple of times a year.

00:10:00.470 --> 00:10:03.480
In order for any, and I've seen this over
the years.

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:07.850
Anybody who does this [remote] very effectively,
anybody who does this typically very, very

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:11.740
effectively, they're very good at accountability,
very good at accountability, which means you're

00:10:11.740 --> 00:10:18.320
very good at communication, but they're also
very, very good at creating tools that allows

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:21.620
them to constantly develop and improve.

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:23.310
So tools could be many different things.

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:24.440
It could be an accountability tool.

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:26.190
It could be a communication tool.

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:27.350
It can be a reference tool.

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:29.500
It can be a, you know, document tool.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:32.360
It can be a tool that tells them how to do
something.

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:34.200
It can be an educational tool.

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:36.700
It can be a Salesforce appointment tool.

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:41.100
There's a lot of tools, note tools, there's
a lot of tools that you can use for everyone

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:42.190
to know what things are doing.

00:10:42.190 --> 00:10:43.190
Calendar tools.

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:44.550
But it's got to be tool driven.

00:10:44.550 --> 00:10:49.470
Google Docs, there's so many different things
that you can use to make it a tool driven

00:10:49.470 --> 00:10:50.470
business.

00:10:50.470 --> 00:10:54.029
And last but not least, a solution to build
remotely is a leaders bulletin.

00:10:54.029 --> 00:10:56.230
I'm a big fan of leaders bulletin.

00:10:56.230 --> 00:10:58.460
I had a staff meeting the other day.

00:10:58.460 --> 00:11:00.029
This was two weeks ago.

00:11:00.029 --> 00:11:01.399
And it was a very intense meeting.

00:11:01.399 --> 00:11:03.140
And this is what the staff meeting was.

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:07.860
I said, I as a CEO, I am useless without numbers.

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:08.860
I don't even exist.

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:10.279
I'm a nobody.

00:11:10.279 --> 00:11:13.889
You may as well fire me and send me home if
I don't have reports.

00:11:13.889 --> 00:11:15.010
I need reports.

00:11:15.010 --> 00:11:16.260
I need figures.

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:17.449
I need trends.

00:11:17.449 --> 00:11:18.589
I need 24 months.

00:11:18.589 --> 00:11:20.860
I need to know what this thing did vs. last
year.

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:22.570
I need to know what this thing did vs. last
month.

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:25.410
I need as much reporting as possible.

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:30.810
The more reports I have, the more I can find
leaks, where we're losing money, or this individual

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:33.329
is not running a proper office that they can
fix.

00:11:33.329 --> 00:11:38.390
So leaders bulletin or reporting allows you
to make the call to that one person that is

00:11:38.390 --> 00:11:40.529
struggling with one area that you can help
